  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Smt. Maya Bai vs Shriram Katarya on 23 February, 2024 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Rajendra Kumar Vani On The 23 rd Of February, 2024 Misc. Appeal No. 6256 of 2023 Between:- 1. Smt. Maya Bai W/O Late Shri Ramji Adiwasi, Aged About 21 Years, Village Bansani Near The Temple (Bansatarkheda) Police Station Damoh Dehat District Damoh (Madhya Pradesh) 2. Paramlal S/O Late Shri Ramji Adiwasi, Aged About 2 Years, Occupation: Minor,Through Natural Guardian Of Mother Smt Maya Bai W/O Late Shri Ramji Adiwasi R/O Village Bansani Near The Temple (Bansatarheda) Police Station Damoh Dehat, District Damoh (Madhya Pradesh) 3. Bhavesh S/O Late Ramji Adiwasi, Aged About 5 Years , Occupation: Through Natural Guardian Of Mother Smt Maya Bai W/O Late Shri Ramji Adiwasi R/O Village Bansani Near The Temple (Bansatarkheda) Police Station Damoh Dehat District Damoh (Madhya Pradesh) 4. Shrimati Muliya Bai W/O Shri Lakhkhu Adiwasi, Aged About 51 Years, R/O Village Bansani Near The Temple (Bansatarkheda) Police Station Damoh Dehat District Damoh (Madhya Pradesh) 5. Lakkhu Adiwasi S/O Shri Parsu Adiwasi, Aged About 56 Years, R/O Village Bansani Near The Temple (Bansatarkheda) Police Station Damoh Dehat District Damoh (Madhya Pradesh) .....Appel (By Ms. Nupur Sullery - Advocate ) And Signature Not Verified Signed by: Akanksha Smt. Maya Bai vs Shriram Katarya on 23 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/130500640/ 1 Maurya Signing time: 07-03-2024 18:19:24 2 1. Shriram Katarya S/O Shri Chain Singh Katarya, Aged About 39 Years, Occupation: Driver Of Offending Vehicle Village Khutiyas Bamhori Police Station Mugawali District Ashiknagar (Madhya Pradesh) 2. Chandrapal Singh Yadav S/O Shri Pahalwan Singh Yadav Occupation: (Owner Of Offending Vehicle Trala No Mp 08Ha0127) R/O Bamnai Haweli Tahsila And District Ashoknagar (Madhya Pradesh) 3. Branch Manager New India Insurance Company Ltd Near Deendayal Hospital Bhairavji Road Regans (Rajasthan) Branch Office, Soloman Complex, Sagar Jabalpur Road Damoh, District Damoh (Insurance Company Of Offencing Vehicle Trala No Mp-08-Ha-0127) (Madhya Pradesh) (By Shri Lalit Joglekar- Advocate For The Respondent No.3/Insurance Company) This appeal coming on for admission this day, th e cour following: Order",
    "facts": "This miscellaneous appeal filed by the appellant under Section 173 of the Motor Vehicle Act, 1988 being aggrieved of award dated 7/7/2023 passed by Motor Accident Claims Tribunal, Damoh in MACC No.04/2022. 2. Due to which he died during treatment. Having heard the learned counsel for the parties and on careful perusal of the record, it is found that Tribunal only assumed income as Rs.5,000/- whereas on the date of accident it was Rs.8700/- per month. But due to increase in income as Rs.8700/- per month instead of Rs.5,000/- the enhancement is more than Rs.1,00,000/- Therefore, the amount of Rs.1,00,000/- may be enhanced in favour of the claimants/appellants.",
    "arguments": "Multiplier applied is also as 17 while it ought to be 18 as looking to age of the deceased, therefore, the award is to be enhanced accordingly."
  },
